      "sample_index": 1,
      "text": "To solve this problem, we need to determine the number of nickels (or dimes or quarters) Jamie has. Let's denote the number of each type of coin by \\( n \\).\n\n1. **Define the value of each type of coin:**\n   - A nickel is worth \\$0.05.\n   - A dime is worth \\$0.10.\n   - A quarter is worth \\$0.25.\n\n2. **Set up the equation for the total value of the coins:**\n   - The total value of the nickels is \\( 0.05n \\).\n   - The total value of the dimes is \\( 0.10n \\).\n   - The total value of the quarters is \\( 0.25n \\).\n\n   The sum of these values is given as \\$13.20. Therefore, we can write the equation:\n   \\[\n   0.05n + 0.10n + 0.25n = 13.20\n   \\]\n\n3. **Combine the terms on the left side:**\n   \\[\n   (0.05 + 0.10 + 0.25)n = 13.20\n   \\]\n\n4. **Calculate the sum of the coefficients:**\n   \\[\n   0.05 + 0.10 + 0.25 = 0.40\n   \\]\n\n   So, the equation simplifies to:\n   \\[\n   0.40n = 13.20\n   \\]\n\n5. **Solve for \\( n \\):**\n   \\[\n   n = \\frac{13.20}{0.40}\n   \\]\n\n6. **Perform the division:**\n   \\[\n   n = 33\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, Jamie has \\(\\boxed{33}\\) nickels.",
